Rendergraphbuilder gives informations about whats needed or not

on whats needed or not rendergraph initializes transient resources, and on submit sets the layout of external images

barriers are created in the builder since they require information across tasks, but view/buffer value are initialized while building the command buffer as it requires information only the rendergraph knows

we don't register by name anymore since we are going to have a lot of tasks that are generated at runtime with materials instances

rendergraph will have a dictionary of createinfo that it can pull on the fly, materialdefs define by name and usage which resources are going to use, whic then are passed to the rendergraphbuilder who builds the actual graph


it's better if the builder explores depthfirst instead of level first




for now I defined that the builder takes in all the tasks, 